# # /cocos/
#
# Cocos: a framework to apply antimicrobial resistance prediction models to
# bacterial sequencing samples. Its registry describes the processing steps and
# prediction models it offers, with the AMRF vocabulary (https://w3id.org/amrf/).
# Source code: https://github.com/DEAL-US/Cocos
#
# Everything under https://w3id.org/cocos/ (the registry, its models and steps,
# the VoID description, the data dump and the SPARQL endpoint) redirects to the
# Cocos deployment, which serves an HTML page or RDF (Turtle, JSON-LD)
# depending on the Accept header.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# María Quirós Quiroga
# mquiros1@us.es
# GitHub username: mquirosq
#
# Daniel Ayala Hernández
# dayala1@us.es
# GitHub username: dayala1
#
# Fernando Sola Espinosa
# fsola@us.es
# GitHub username: fersolesp

RewriteEngine on

# SPARQL endpoint: 307 so that POST queries keep their method and body
RewriteRule ^sparql$ https://gin.us.es/cocos/sparql [R=307,L]

# The registry, its models and steps, and everything else
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://gin.us.es/cocos/$1 [R=303,L]
